<title>GREECE: TABLE OF GREEK MUTUAL FUND FLOWS, ASSETS.</title>
<headline>TABLE OF GREEK MUTUAL FUND FLOWS, ASSETS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ionian Bank reported the</p>
<p>following daily and year-to-date changes in the volume of Greek</p>
<p>mutual fund outstanding shares, net assets and net share prices,</p>
<p>as well as total net asset sizes as of June 4.</p>
<p>				    June 4/June 3   June 4/Dec 31, 96</p>
<p>						 (%)		  (%)</p>
<p>NET SHARE PRICES*</p>
<p>  Total market			    0.09		 6.99</p>
<p>  Fixed income &amp;money market funds  0.03		 5.17</p>
<p>  International funds		   0.01		10.12</p>
<p>  Growth Funds			   -0.69		57.70</p>
<p>* Prices include distributed dividends</p>
<p>VOLUME OF SHARES</p>
<p>  Total market			    0.48		31.89</p>
<p>  Fixed income &amp;money market funds  0.48		32.40</p>
<p>  International funds		   0.22		12.32</p>
<p>  Growth funds			    0.77		29.32</p>
<p>NET ASSETS</p>
<p>  Total market			    0.48		39.42</p>
<p>  Fixed income &amp;money market funds  0.50		37.77</p>
<p>  International funds		   0.26		21.19</p>
<p>  Growth funds			    0.13		99.63</p>
<p>All calculations are based on a performance index of mutual</p>
<p>funds whose base was set to be equal to 100 on December 31,</p>
<p>1991.</p>
<p>NET ASSET SIZES (in drachmas)</p>
<p>  Total market				  5,302,280,567,992</p>
<p>  Fixed income funds			  1,933,621,196,113</p>
<p>  Money market funds			  3,028,486,764,341</p>
<p>  International funds			    95,269,097,423</p>
<p>  Growth funds				    244,903,510,115</p>
<p>--Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
